I think you're right - the speed of the CPU is MUCH more important than
the amount of free RAM.  On my 486/33, moves can be made as fast as you
can type.  Eg, hold down a cursor key and the man moves at the keyboard
auto-repeat rate.  Whether I have 500k or 600k memory free really doesn't
seem to matter.

